  "raw_reviews": [
    {
      "review_id": "22638",
      "reviewbody": "I had this on vinyl many years ago and it was played until it could be played no more.  I would be \"grateful\" if the whole show was available.  The Uncle John's Band is a classic version.\n\nWhat is here is very good.  The sound quality is extremely good. The vocals are excellent!  Lesh is a driving force on all songs.  Garcia is a little low in the mix on Hard to Handle, but not on the other tunes.\n\nGiven the incomplete nature of the recording, I need to give it 4 stars. What is here is 5 star material.\n\nDoes anyone know where to get the rest of the songs?",
      "reviewtitle": "May I Please Have The Whole Show?",
      "reviewer": "Carpe Diem",
      "reviewdate": "2004-10-11 16:31:54",
      "createdate": "2004-10-11 16:31:54",
      "stars": "4"
    },
    {
      "review_id": "38944",
      "reviewbody": "Controversy swirls around this setlist.  Here's the setlist for this date from Bear's cassettes:\n\n1. Me and Bobby McGee \n2. Dire Wolf \n3. Good Lovin' \n4. Drums \n5. Good Lovin' \n6. Casey Jones \n7. Uncle John's Band \n\nDick Latavla has been quoted \"This is how it exists on Bear's cassettes, I can't be responsible for how Deadbase has the songs listed.\"\n\nThis setlist also circulates in SBD format but does not appear in the Archive.",
      "reviewtitle": "Is this really 12/23 or is it 12/17??",
      "reviewer": "headgdhead",
      "reviewdate": "2005-04-18 04:57:55",
      "createdate": "2005-04-18 04:57:55",
      "stars": "4"
    },
